---
description: Visual snapshot catalog, runner, and review.html workflow
globs: tests/snapshot-tests/**
alwaysApply: false
---
- Catalog: `tests/snapshot-tests/model/<suite>/<slug>/<slug>.manifest.json`. Suites are `retail`, `classic`, and `mount` (`catalog.ts`). `case` (base, weapons, size, optional mount / `textureBaking`) lives in that manifest. `textureBaking` is required for bake cases.
- Retail and mount use the local `wow` product. Classic uses `wow_classic`. The runner switches the loaded product and restores the one it found at start.
- Clear exported assets between products: identical texture paths can have different bytes in Retail and Classic. Raw cache clearing alone does not isolate exported textures.
- Run with `bun run test:snapshot` against the converter already listening at `WOW_CONVERTER_URL` or `http://127.0.0.1:3001`. One case: `SNAPSHOT_SUITE=retail SNAPSHOT_SLUG=<slug> bun test tests/snapshot-tests/model/model.test.ts`. `bun test` does not forward arguments after `--`.
- Update with `bun run test:snapshot-update` (`SNAPSHOT_UPDATE=1`). One case: `$env:SNAPSHOT_UPDATE='1'; $env:SNAPSHOT_SUITE='retail'; $env:SNAPSHOT_SLUG='<slug>'; bun test tests/snapshot-tests/model/model.test.ts` (PowerShell). Unix: prefix env vars. Update rewrites the expected image and the recorded sequence. It keeps `diff.thresholdPercent` and `diff.channelDelta`.
- A snapshot run writes `review.html` (wowhead | expected | actual). This HTML page is for human review of the test results: dropdown defaults to failed; switch to successful. Plain Wowhead URL cases without attached weapons/mounts capture `<slug>.wowhead.png` and use `shot.cameras` for expected/actual. `shot.wowheadPairHash` pairs the PNG, cameras, URL and exact source animation; missing/stale pairs are recaptured. Source capture failures fail the case. Use export metadata `wowName`/`wowVariant` and fresh `modelScale`, never infer units from mesh bounds. 👍/👎 sorts into good/bad (bad asks for a comment); Copy results. Rebuild with `bun tests/snapshot-tests/model/write-review.ts`, or pass `suite/slug` args.
- Case files live in `tests/snapshot-tests/model/<suite>/<slug>/`, including `<slug>.actual.png`, `<slug>.diff.png`, and `<slug>.expected-prev.png`. Those three plus `review.html` and `review-failures.json` are gitignored.
- Eligible paired shots preserve Wowhead framing. Other cases fit mesh vertices to 92% of the tile on the limiting axis; a top view fits the footprint.
- The sheet is 2×3, tile 640×400: front, left, back / right, top, bottom. A pixel counts when its largest channel change is greater than `channelDelta` (default 4). Fail when counted/sheet exceeds `thresholdPercent` (default 1). A sequence other than `shot.sequence` also fails. A missing expected image fails; do not create one on a compare run.
- `<slug>.diff.png` is black where the sheets match. A changed pixel is red, and a larger channel change is a stronger red. Read it on failure. After an intentional change, update that slug and review the new expected image before committing it.
- Preserve approved baselines during refactors. A failed comparison is evidence to investigate, not a reason to set `SNAPSHOT_UPDATE=1` or relax thresholds. For visual bug fixes, follow `debug-wowhead-mismatch` for paired proof and its existing baseline-approval workflow.
- Reported models that do not have an approved sheet yet have an `issue` string in the manifest, `<slug>.reference.png` (the wow.export shot), and `<slug>.reported.png` (the shot of our export from that report). Compare still writes `<slug>.actual.png` and does not pixel-diff them. Compare `actual.png` to `reference.png`. A full update does not write `expected.png` for those cases. Set `SNAPSHOT_SLUG` to approve that sheet.
